{
  "an6.10:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 6.10 ",
  "an6.10:0.2": "1. Worthy of Offerings ",
  "an6.10:0.3": "With Mahānāma ",
  "an6.10:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying in the land of the Sakyans, near Kapilavatthu in the Banyan Tree Monastery. ",
  "an6.10:1.2": "Then Mahānāma the Sakyan went up to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him: ",
  "an6.10:1.3": "“Sir, when a noble disciple has reached the fruit and understood the instructions, what kind of meditation do they frequently practice?” ",
  "an6.10:2.1": "“Mahānāma, when a noble disciple has reached the fruit and understood the instructions they frequently practice this kind of meditation. ",
  "an6.10:2.2": "Firstly, a noble disciple recollects the Realized One: ",
  "an6.10:2.3": "‘That Blessed One is perfected, a fully awakened Buddha, accomplished in knowledge and conduct, holy, knower of the world, supreme guide for those fit for training, teacher of gods and humans, awakened, blessed.’ ",
  "an6.10:2.4": "When a noble disciple recollects the Realized One their mind is not full of greed, hate, and delusion. ",
  "an6.10:2.5": "At that time their mind is quite unswerving, based on the Realized One. ",
  "an6.10:2.6": "A noble disciple whose mind is unswerving finds inspiration in the meaning and the teaching, and finds joy connected with the teaching. ",
  "an6.10:2.7": "When they’re joyful, rapture springs up. When the mind is full of rapture, the body becomes tranquil. When the body is tranquil, they feel 